<mujoco model="skydio_x2_include">
  <!--
    This is a THIN WRAPPER, not a re-derivation of the drone body.

    I don't have your actual landing-project Skydio X2 MJCF (mass, inertia,
    rotor placement, actuator defs, velocity-lag params) in my context here:
    only summaries of the conversation that built it. Rather than guess at
    those numbers and risk silently drifting from the physics you already
    validated closed-loop in Gazebo/PX4 SITL, point this file at your real one.

    CONFIRMED: mujoco_menagerie lives inside flow_matching_following/, and
    you load `mujoco_menagerie/skydio_x2/scene.xml` directly today. Critical
    detail: scene.xml is NOT a bare robot body: it bundles its own
    <worldbody> with a skybox, checkered groundplane, a directional light,
    and a static landing_marker box. Including scene.xml here would collide
    with the scenes already built (two floors, two lights, a leftover
    landing-project marker that isn't the moving AprilTag target Phase 1
    needs).

    So this wrapper includes x2.xml directly instead: that's the bare
    actuated robot body scene.xml itself includes, without the competing
    worldbody. This should compose cleanly with scene_warehouse/courtyard/
    urban.xml, each of which defines its own floor/lights/skybox.

    Camera note, still open: I don't have x2.xml's contents, so I can't
    confirm whether it already defines a camera site, and if so, what it's
    mounted/oriented as. Phase 1 needs a front-facing, pitch-only camera
    (no yaw toward target, per your correction earlier). If x2.xml has no
    camera defined, or has one mounted differently, that needs adding/fixing
    here; flagged as open below rather than guessed.
  -->

  <include file="../../mujoco_menagerie/skydio_x2/x2.xml"/>

  <!--
    If your landing project's drone body does NOT already define a pitching
    camera site/joint (likely true, since landing used a fixed overhead-ish
    view per earlier discussion), add a hinge joint for camera pitch here,
    e.g.:

      <body name="camera_mount" pos="0.1 0 -0.02">
        <joint name="camera_pitch" type="hinge" axis="0 1 0"
               range="-90 10" damping="0.5"/>
        <camera name="front_cam" mode="fixed" fovy="90"/>
      </body>

    as a child of the drone base body; adjust pos/range once we see the
    actual body tree. Left unimplemented here since it depends on the real
    body structure I don't have visibility into yet.
  -->
</mujoco>